<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eva Perón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Evita, Eva Duarte de Perón</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eva Perón, known as Evita, was an Argentine actress who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-peron">Juan Perón</a> in 1945 and became the most powerful woman in Argentine politics as first lady. Through her foundation she ran a vast programme of social aid, and she championed the women's suffrage law of 1947 and the women's branch of the Peronist party. Her death from cancer at thirty-three made her a lasting popular icon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eva-peron.jpg" alt="Eva Perón" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pinélides Fusco · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evita_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
